{{inh+|en|enm|cold}}, from {{inh|en|ang-ang|cald}}. The West Saxon form, {{m|ang|ċeald|t=cold}}, survived as early Middle English {{m|enm|cheald}}, {{m|enm|cheld}}{{,}} or {{m|enm|chald}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|code=36101}}</ref> Both descended from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kald}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kaldaz|t=cold}}, a participle form of {{m|gem-pro|*kalaną|t=to be cold, to freeze}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gel-|t=to be cold, to freeze}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|cauld|t=cold}}, {{cog|stq|koold|t=cold}}, {{cog|fy|kâld|t=cold}}, {{cog|gsw|chalt}}, {{m|gsw|choalt}}, {{m|gsw|cholt}}, {{m|gsw|chélte|t=cold}}, {{cog|bar|ckolt}}, {{m|bar|kholt}}, {{m|bar|koid}}, {{m|bar|kòlt|t=cold}}, {{cog|gmw-cfr|kalt|t=cold}}, {{cog|cim|kalt}}, {{m|cim|khalt|t=cold}}, {{cog|nl|koud|t=cold}}, {{cog|de|kalt|t=cold}}, {{cog|nds|kold}}, {{m|nds|koolt|t=cold}}, {{cog|lb|kal|t=cold}}, {{cog|mhn|khòlt}}, {{m|mhn|kòlt|t=cold}}, {{cog|wym|kāłt|t=cold}}, {{cog|yi|קאַלט|t=cold}}, {{cog|da|kold|t=cold}}, {{cog|fo,is|kaldur|t=cold}}, {{cog|nb|kald|t=cold}}, {{cog|nn|kald}}, {{m|nn|kald’u|t=cold}}, {{cog|sv|kall|t=cold}}, {{cog|got|𐌺𐌰𐌻𐌳𐍃|t=cold}}; also {{cog|la|gelū}}, {{m|la|gelum}}, {{m|la|gelus|t=frost; chill, cold}}, {{cog|be|хо́лад|t=cold}}, {{cog|bg|хлад|t=chill, coolness}}, {{cog|cs|chlad|t=cold}}, {{cog|mk|лад|t=shade; coolness}}, {{cog|pl|chłód|t=cold}}, {{cog|ru,uk|хо́лод|t=cold}}, {{cog|sh|хла̑д}}, {{m|sh|hlȃd|t=shade}}, {{cog|sa|जड|t=cold; stiff}}, {{m|sa|जल|t=water}}. Related to {{m|en|cool}}.
