===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|comb}}, from {{inh|en|ang|camb||comb}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kamb}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kambaz||comb}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*ǵómbʰos||tooth}}, a {{doublet|nocap=1|en|cam}}. The verb is derived from the noun and displaced the older verb {{m|en|kemb}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Compare {{cog|stq|Koum}}, Swedish/Dutch {{m|nl|kam}}, {{cog|da|kam}}, {{cog|no|kam}}, {{cog|de|Kamm}}; also {{cog|txb|keme}}, {{cog|lt|žam̃bas||sharp edge}}, {{cog|cu|зѫбъ|sc=Cyrs}}, {{cog|sq|dhëmb}}, {{cog|grc|γομφίος||backtooth, molar}}, {{cog|sa|जम्भ}}).
