===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|clucchen}}, {{m|enm|clicchen}}, {{m|enm|cluchen}}, {{m|enm|clechen}}, {{m|enm|cleken}}, from {{inh|en|ang|clyċċan|t=to clutch, clench}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*klukkjan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*klukjaną}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*klu-|t=to ball up, conglomerate, amass}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*glew-|t=to ball up; lump, mass}}.
Cognate with {{cog|sv|klyka||clamp, fork, branch}}. The noun is from {{der|en|enm|cleche}}, {{m|enm|cloche}}, {{m|enm|cloke}} {{gloss|"claw, talon, hand"; compare {{cog|sco|cleuk}}, {{m|sco|cluke}}, {{m|sco|cluik||claw, talon}}}}, of uncertain origin, with the form probably assimilated to the verb.

Alternative etymology derives {{cog|ang|clyċċan}} from {{der|en|gem-pro|*klēk-||claw, hand}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*glēk-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ǵlēḱ-||claw, hand; to clutch, snatch}}. If so, then cognate with {{cog|ga|glac||hand}}.

