##* {{RQ:Plutarch Holland Morals|chapter=Of the Nouriture and Education of Children|page=15|passage=To be ſhort, a wretched and curſed generation they be; hypocrites, pretending friendſhip, but they can not skill of plaine dealing and franke ſpeech. Rich men they '''claw''', ſooth up and flatter: the poore they contemne and despiſe.}}
